        optionFeedback: [`Selectins and their ligands are expressed on leukocytes and activated endothelial cells and mediate low-affinity interactions that form and are broken by the shear force of flowing blood. Because of these interactions, the leukocytes roll along the endothelium at sites of inflammation. This is the first step in the passage of leukocytes from the circulation into tissues, and it gives them the chance to initiate the second step of firm attachment (mediated by integrins). `,`Integrins are involved in firm adhesion of leukocytes to endothelium.`,`Leukotriene B<sub>4</sub> is a chemotactic agent. `,`NADPH oxidase catalyzes the generation of reactive oxygen species, part of the respiratory burst. `,`Defensins are antimicrobial peptides stored in leukocyte granules.`],
