        q: `Two weeks after an acute myocardial infarction, the necrotic myocardium has largely been replaced by capillaries, fibroblasts, and collagen. A variety of inflammatory cells are present. Which of the following inflammatory cell types in such a lesion plays an important part at this point in the healing process?`,
